capability request/client-address  the client's address, through proxies the program trusts
  heroes  web.forwarded_of, web.trusted_networks, web.Forwarded
  go      echo.Context.RealIP, echo.ExtractIPDirect, ExtractIPFromXFFHeader, ExtractIPFromRealIPHeader, echo.TrustOption, gin.Context.ClientIP, gin.Context.RemoteIP, gin.Engine.SetTrustedProxies, chi/middleware.RealIP
  rust    -
  python  flask.Request.remote_addr, flask.Request.access_route, werkzeug.middleware.proxy_fix.ProxyFix
  note    `X-Forwarded-For` read only from an address the program trusts, from its last entry back; `forwarded_of` trusts networks (`10.0.0.0/8`) as well as addresses, prefers RFC 7239's `Forwarded`, whose element of the client gives its `proto` and `host`, and else takes the last value of `X-Forwarded-Proto` and `X-Forwarded-Host`, the nearest proxy's, as werkzeug's `ProxyFix` with one hop reads them; ProxyFix and Echo's `TrustOption` count hops or ranges, gin's `SetTrustedProxies` takes networks as here; the client is the first hop from the nearest back that no trusted network holds, so fields a client writes name only hops behind it

