  rust    -
  python  -
  note    a token bucket per client key, as golang.org/x/time/rate keeps one, observed with its v0.16.0 on 2026-11-17: a burst of 3 at 2 a second allowed three, refused the fourth with a delay of 500 ms, refused a nanosecond before it and allowed at it; a refused request leaves the bucket as it was and a time before its last token counts none, as Go's; the wait is rounded up to the nanosecond where Go truncates (333.333334 ms against 333.333333 at 3 a second), so waiting it always finds a token; the time is the caller's, never a clock read here; 429 says Echo's words, "rate limit exceeded", with `Retry-After` in whole seconds rounded up, which Echo does not send; a full bucket is forgotten, losing nothing, and past `most_keys` the older half, where Echo's memory store forgets a visitor after `ExpiresIn` and holds no bound; a step the program calls with its own `@` limiter, since a step `before` calls takes none

